      {
        "id": "Initiative Proposition Number One",
        "title": "People's Initiative to Limit Property Tax in Wyoming through a Homeowner's Property Exemption",
        "summary": "This citizen initiative would exempt 50% of the assessed value of a qualified homeowner's primary residence from property tax, with no more than one exemption per property or per owner each year. To qualify, a homeowner must have lived in Wyoming for at least a year and in the home for at least six months of the prior tax year, file a sworn claim with the county assessor by the fourth Monday in May, and confirm eligibility each year after; false claims carry a penalty. The state's estimated revenue loss is about $92.6 million in fiscal year 2028 and $95.9 million in fiscal year 2029, not counting effects on local governments.",
        "yesMeans": "You vote FOR enacting the 50% homeowner's property tax exemption for primary residences.",
        "noMeans": "You vote AGAINST the initiative, and current property tax law is unchanged.",
